d this is really the sustainable way  to deliver long-term benefit including  increased network deployment  what we note what we noticed that  there's not enough in terms of  take up of the new instruments  there are new provisions in the code  that directly address the issue of  voluntary cooperation  between network providers  and if cooperation really  can be effectively deployed  then we will see much more investments  regulators have not to be shy in  deploying these new tools  companies have to embrace these new  tools through cooperation through  agreements  we can actually speed up network  deployment it's a new form of  cooperation in regulation between  regulated party regulators that the code  very much sponsors and we would like to  see much more that what we have seen so  far  when it comes to spectrum  we also  tried to deliver a very ambitious  regulatory framework  with the obligation of member state to  make available binary band for fixed and  mobile 5g fixed 5g is really now  taking  quite some traction in some member  states  and we need of course the spectrum to be  made available  and also we have established a very  light regulatory regime for small cell  deployment that's very important for  hybrid forms of 5g and wi-5 and to  facilitate network specifications  thinking for instance at  6g  so far we have not seen a lot of  innovation in this respect and really i  invite  companies to make use of such a  simplified regulatory framework  of course we will work more and more to  make sure  that there are no red tapes that impede  connectivity that's why the new  connectivity infrastructure act will  result in even  better  fight if you like to red tapes  we need to make sure that the  the new connected reactor will replace  the broadband cost reduction directive  and we need to be sure that really fiber  can be quickly deployed everywhere  and where there are burdens  which result from bureaucracy this have  to go  so that's the the purpose of 